{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvoUxT8yvW9SQMTeRHCV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Foujd4JoJtFVezvvi2u6nU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; cat > paper_strategy.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"selected_prompt_family\": \"paper_standalone\",\n  \"recommended_title\": \"When Is One Kernel SHAP Run Enough? Predicting Top-3 Attribution Reproducibility from a Single Budgeted Run\",\n  \"central_question\": \"For a trained tabular classifier explained by a budget-limited Kernel SHAP run, how often does the single run's top-3 feature set agree with independent reruns, and can that agreement be predicted from the single run's own coalition data better than trivial and split-half baselines?\",\n  \"central_thesis\": \"Single-run Kernel SHAP top-3 reproducibility is conditional rather than uniformly high (mean agreement 0.807 at a 4d coalition budget vs 0.932 at 16d on the held-out evaluation datasets), and a diagnostic computed only from the assessed run predicts it with lower squared error than always-reliable, constant-0.5 and split-half-gap baselines, but only modestly above a pairing-permuted control, so most of its skill is budget-level calibration and per-instance resolution is limited (Spearman 0.58).\",\n  \"narrative_rationale\": \"The final evaluation completed with outcome qualified (final.qualification.outcome), with positive lower confidence bounds against all three evaluator baselines and against the permuted-pairing control, so a measured-results paper is supportable. The artifacts do not support the original brief's broad empirical study (no per-dataset/per-model breakdown, no background-size or retraining-noise experiments, no deep tabular models, no ablation_studies). The strongest coherent story is therefore a bounded one: define single-run reproducibility operationally (top-3 Jaccard against 8 reruns), show it depends on coalition budget, and evaluate a single-run self-diagnostic against honest baselines and a control, stating loudly that the gain over the control is small. This is thesis-first and avoids the three-attempt search chronology; search is demoted to a short supplementary robustness note because there are no ablations that attribute the gain to components.\",\n  \"prior_paper_story_status\": \"rejected\",\n  \"edit_framing_decision\": \"Not edit mode: no previous_paper directory or edit-context files exist. Fresh framing; no prior thesis to preserve.\",\n  \"staged_input_impact\": [\n    \"No staged prior manuscript or new-program inputs; framing derives only from paper_data.json (final_evaluation, result.* search sources), task/task_contract.json, and evaluator source for the label/baseline definitions.\",\n    \"paper_data.json has no downstream_study key, so no downstream-study comparison is planned.\"\n  ],\n  \"method_groups\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Single-run reproducibility label (measurement protocol)\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Defines the object being predicted: for each explained instance, mean top-3 Jaccard agreement between the assessed Kernel SHAP run and 8 independent reruns, at coalition budgets 4d and 16d, background 32 rows, three model families (logistic regression, random forest, sklearn MLP). Needed to state the conditional-reliability claim (final.metric.mean_label_low_budget / mean_label_high_budget).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Single-run self-diagnostic (frozen selected configuration)\",\n      \"role\": \"proposed\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"The studied method: from one run's coalition masks, weights and values it simulates reruns via a delete-one-group jackknife (4 partitions, antithetic common-random-number draws), shrinks toward a budget-dependent prior and adds a small margin gate, outputting r_hat in [0,1]. Constants are hand-set and untuned; say so.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Evaluator-owned reference baselines\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Always-reliable (r=1), constant 0.5, and a split-half-gap heuristic computed from the same single run. Grounded via final.metric.skill_vs_always_reliable, skill_vs_constant_half, skill_vs_gap_heuristic and their CI lows. The original search-time baseline program has no grounded score in paper_data, so that comparison is omitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Label-permuted pairing control\",\n      \"role\": \"ablation\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Shuffles which r_hat is paired with which instance label (20 deterministic derangements) to separate budget/cell-level calibration from instance-specific information. Score 0.9701 vs diagnostic 0.9838 (final.metric.control_permuted_score, combined_minus_control_ci_low). The key calibration guard of the paper.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Search-plane model variants (three configurations)\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Supplement-only: three scored configurations on search datasets (result.improvement_001..003) show the selection and that differences are small; no component ablations exist, so no mechanistic attribution is claimed. All 3 attempts were scored; there are no unscored attempts.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"results_focus\": [\n    \"Conditional reliability: final mean label 0.8065 at 4d vs 0.9315 at 16d budget (final.metric.mean_label_low_budget, mean_label_high_budget); single-run top-3 set reproducibility is not uniformly high, and the low-budget regime is where one run is least trustworthy. Do not break this down by dataset or model family; no grounded breakdown exists.\",\n    \"Diagnostic accuracy on final data: combined score 0.9838 (= 1 - mean squared error, so MSE about 0.0162; derived arithmetic, label it derived) with seed-level scores 0.9850 and 0.9826 (final.evidence.episodes, seeds 9001/9002).\",\n    \"Skill over baselines with one-sided 2.5th-percentile bootstrap lower bounds: vs always-reliable +0.0353 (low 0.0171), vs constant 0.5 +0.1543 (low 0.1245), vs split-half gap heuristic +0.0122 (low 0.0081). Only lower bounds are available; do not fabricate upper bounds or symmetric intervals.\",\n    \"Honest control: permuted-pairing score 0.9701; diagnostic minus control = 0.0137 (derived), lower bound 0.0101. Interpret as real but small instance-specific information on top of budget-level calibration; Spearman between r_hat and label 0.581 indicates moderate ranking ability.\",\n    \"Scale of the gain in plain terms: root-mean-squared error about 0.127 for the diagnostic vs about 0.227 for always-reliable (both derived from grounded metrics; label as derived).\",\n    \"Selection is reported separately from the final evaluation: search scores 0.9760, 0.9837, 0.9854 for three scored configurations on the search datasets; the frozen selected configuration is the 0.9854 one. Per-attempt two-seed ranges overlap, so the ordering is not claimed significant.\",\n    \"Final outcome is qualified (final.qualification.outcome); no failed-qualification disclosure needed, but qualification does not turn these bounded metrics into general validity claims.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_plan\": [\n    \"Fig. 1 (overview, early): the measurement protocol and claim structure at a glance: trained model + instance -> one assessed Kernel SHAP run at budget 4d or 16d -> diagnostic outputs r_hat; evaluator reruns 8 times -> top-3 Jaccard label; scoring against always-reliable, constant 0.5, split-half gap, permuted control.\",\n    \"Fig. 2 (main evidence, two panels): (a) skill (MSE reduction) over always-reliable, constant 0.5, split-half gap heuristic, and over permuted control, with one-sided bootstrap lower-bound markers; (b) mean single-run top-3 agreement at 4d vs 16d budget.\",\n    \"Table 1 (native LaTeX): final metrics with lower bounds, seed-level scores and the derived MSE/RMSE column marked as derived.\",\n    \"Supplement Fig./Table: search-plane scores of the three configurations with per-seed values (supporting only).\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_specs\": [\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"protocol_overview\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Give glance value for the setting: what a single run is, what the label measures (top-3 Jaccard vs 8 reruns), what the diagnostic sees, and what it is scored against.\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"group_by\": \"protocol_stage\",\n      \"metric\": \"none (conceptual)\",\n      \"split_by\": \"none\",\n      \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n      \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"layout_rationale\": \"ICLR style is single-column (text width about 5.5 in); a left-to-right pipeline with 4-5 boxes and short labels needs the full text width to keep text at or above about 7 pt. Place on page 1 or 2.\",\n      \"allow_progression\": false,\n      \"max_panels\": 1,\n      \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n      \"max_series_per_panel\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"main_comparison\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Show (a) diagnostic skill over each baseline and over the permuted control with lower-bound markers and (b) budget-conditional single-run agreement.\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"two_panel_bar\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"group_by\": \"comparator\",\n      \"metric\": \"final.metric.skill_vs_* ; combined minus control; mean_label_low/high_budget\",\n      \"split_by\": \"panel (skill vs budget label)\",\n      \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n      \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"layout_rationale\": \"Two side-by-side panels with 4 and 2 categories and rotated or wrapped labels need text width in the single-column template; column-width does not exist, and shrinking would make labels illegible. Export PDF plus 300-DPI PNG from source.\",\n      \"allow_progression\": false,\n      \"max_panels\": 2,\n      \"max_categories_per_panel\": 4,\n      \"max_series_per_panel\": 2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"supplementary_plan\": {\n    \"purpose\": \"Add reproducibility and robustness depth that supports but is not essential to the central thesis: evaluation protocol details, full metric table, search-plane variant comparison, and the diagnostic's constants and provenance.\",\n    \"planned_subsections\": [\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Evaluation protocol and reproducibility details\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Datasets (German credit partition B, ACS income CA 2018 sample of 20000 rows, Give Me Some Credit sample of 20000 rows; search datasets German partition A and Pima), models, 20 instances per episode, 8 reruns, 20 derangements, 200 bootstrap replicates, final seeds 9001/9002, software versions, hash-based disjointness of search and final data; taken from task_contract.json, resources manifests and evaluator source, with numeric results tied to final.* ids.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\", \"final.qualification.status\", \"final.qualification.outcome\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Full final metric table and derived quantities\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"All final metrics including combined score, skills, lower bounds, permuted control, label means, Spearman; derivation of MSE and RMSE from combined score and skills, shown as arithmetic.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.combined_score\", \"final.metric.control_permuted_score\", \"final.metric.skill_vs_always_reliable\", \"final.metric.skill_vs_always_reliable_ci_low\", \"final.metric.skill_vs_constant_half\", \"final.metric.skill_vs_constant_half_ci_low\", \"final.metric.skill_vs_gap_heuristic\", \"final.metric.skill_vs_gap_heuristic_ci_low\", \"final.metric.combined_minus_control_ci_low\", \"final.metric.spearman_r_hat_vs_label\", \"final.metric.mean_label_low_budget\", \"final.metric.mean_label_high_budget\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Candidate configurations considered on the search datasets\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Three scored configurations (full-covariance jackknife with inflation; variance-reduced simulation with hand-set calibration; budget-prior shrinkage with partition ensemble) with search scores and per-seed values; states 3 of 3 attempts scored, no component ablation available, ordering not claimed significant.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\"result.improvement_001\", \"result.improvement_002\", \"result.improvement_003\", \"result.top_program_01\", \"result.top_program_02\", \"result.top_program_03\", \"result.total_attempts\", \"result.total_evaluated_programs\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Diagnostic constants and their provenance\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Hand-set, untuned constants (budget prior 0.84/0.96 taken from search-plane budget-wise label means, simulation weight 0.6, margin boost 0.02, 4 partitions); the prior was derived from search data whose label means (0.840/0.958) differ from final (0.807/0.932), a likely source of mild miscalibration. Source for numbers is the program notes; flag as method description, not a metric.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\"result.best_correct_score\", \"final.metric.mean_label_low_budget\", \"final.metric.mean_label_high_budget\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"forbidden_headings\": [\n    \"Search Progression\",\n    \"Milestones\",\n    \"First Valid Result\",\n    \"Campaign Phases\",\n    \"Cycle 1 / Cycle 2 / Cycle 3\",\n    \"Experiment A / Experiment B\",\n    \"Run Log\",\n    \"What We Tried\"\n  ],\n  \"forbidden_phrases\": [\n    \"correctness rate\",\n    \"correct and eligible\",\n    \"combined_score\",\n    \"eligible\",\n    \"rubric\",\n    \"state of the art\",\n    \"outperforms prior work\",\n    \"SHAP is reliable\",\n    \"SHAP is unreliable\",\n    \"generalizes to all tabular models\",\n    \"first valid\",\n    \"incumbent\"\n  ],\n  \"notes_for_writer\": [\n    \"Stay inside the bounded claim: Kernel SHAP with interventional value function, 32-row background, budgets 4d and 16d, k=3, three model families, three final datasets, 20 instances per episode, 8 reruns. The task brief's broader items (background-size effects, retraining noise, deep tabular models, other explainers, leverage-score estimators) were not run; list them as not done, not as findings.\",\n    \"Present the reproducibility label as the primary scientific object and the diagnostic as the tool evaluated; the title and abstract should name the mechanism (single-run self-diagnostic of Kernel SHAP top-3 reproducibility) and the setting.\",\n    \"Never write combined_score in the paper; call it 'score = 1 - mean squared error of r_hat against the agreement label' and describe aggregation as instance -> seed -> model/budget cell -> dataset equal-weight means.\",\n    \"Uncertainty: only the final seed-level scores (two seeds) and one-sided 2.5th-percentile paired-bootstrap lower bounds exist. Say so. Do not draw error bars the artifacts cannot support; lower bounds can be drawn as markers.\",\n    \"Frame the permuted control as the main limitation-aware result: 0.9701 vs 0.9838 shows most skill is budget/cell-level calibration. State this in the abstract.\",\n    \"The diagnostic's budget prior was set from search-plane label means; final label means are lower, so say miscalibration at the margin is plausible but not measured.\",\n    \"Per-dataset and per-family conclusions are not grounded; do not state any, and name this as a limitation. The 4d vs 16d label gap is an aggregate across datasets and families.\",\n    \"The selected configuration's constants were hand-set and untuned, and diagnostics trust is marked unverified in the evaluation evidence; disclose. No component ablation exists, so do not attribute gains to jackknife, partition ensembling, shrinkage or margin gate individually.\",\n    \"Do not cite the original search-time baseline program's score; it has no grounded source id. Use evaluator-owned baselines instead.\",\n    \"References: references.bib is largely irrelevant (e.g., forest carbon, UHPC strength, soil moisture entries) and must not be cited. Relevant retrieved entries are Covert2020ImprovingKP, Gupte2025UnderstandingTB, Mitchell2021SamplingPF (and possibly Petrosian2024ExplainableAE after checking). Starter literature (Lundberg and Lee 2017, Krishna 2022, Nogueira 2018, Webber 2010, Musco and Witter 2024, Chen 2020, Ding 2021) is missing from the bib; re-run retrieve-references for those titles before citing, otherwise cite only what exists and do not invent entries.\",\n    \"Body budget is 8 to 9 pages with no padding. Spend space on: problem framing (why one run is common practice and what could go wrong), formal definitions (Kernel SHAP with budgeted coalitions, top-3 Jaccard label, scoring metrics), a clear method section for the diagnostic with enough detail to reimplement, the evaluation protocol rationale, results with Table 1 and Fig. 2, a sharp limitation and scope section, and related work. If the evidence cannot honestly fill the page minimum, do not pad; flag the shortfall.\",\n    \"Fig. 1 is the single concept figure (generate-concept-figure); Fig. 2 uses matplotlib, vector PDF in LaTeX, 300-DPI PNG fallback. Both full text width because the template is single-column. Fig. 1 should appear on page 1 or 2.\",\n    \"Anonymize: no author, repo link or lab info; include the LLM Usage section (may be in appendix) and the venue checklist if the template requires it.\",\n    \"Final outcome is qualified; report it plainly, without upgrading it to claims of validity, generality or superiority beyond the evaluated baselines.\",\n    \"Use reader-facing terms 'model variant', 'configuration', 'seeded run' as in the presentation contract; avoid 'program', 'idea', 'eligible'.\"\n  ],\n  \"failure_reason\": \"\"\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('paper_strategy.json'));print('ok')\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":73642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":347},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa2be56c-b52a-4469-b0e1-ffde30ddac4b","uuid":"a1c1aa4a-eb29-4ce0-abb4-5199958035c8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:11:40.060Z","request_id":"req_011CgvoUwue5ZgTik2MdFP9o"}
